      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Taking ibuprofen with food significantly reduces the risk of stomach irritation, which is a good precaution. However, even with Omeprazole and food, exceeding standard recommended doses like 400mg or 600mg without medical guidance is risky and can lead to other side effects beyond stomach discomfort. For strong pain relief, the doctor needs to assess your specific health profile to safely recommend a dosage or alternative. Please prioritize calling a professional as soon as your work allows.",
